> i use  tru64 4.0F on ES40
> when i send files by ftp from WindowsMSDOS-BOX
> to my alpha all files will created with 644 . but i need 664 .

I'm not sure if the stock ftp daemon supports `site umask ...' as
issued from the client (doubt it), but since an ftp session never
starts a shell for you, it doesn't read any personal init files
so setting your umask there won't work.

In general the way to fix this is to change the default umask that
ftpd uses, see the man page for ftpd to learn about the `-u' flag.
Note that this is a system-wide setting though.  Remember to
HUP or restart inetd after you modify the line for ftpd, so inetd
sees any changes you've made.

Tim
