> the blue default background.

> Has anybody some expierience with this problem?

The README.Tru64 file says that you need the OSFMITxxx subset installed
for the dcopserver to run properly. The dcopserver needs the iceauth
program from this subset. Check that this program is available at your
site. It usually sits in /usr/bin/X11.

Also check that your $HOME directory is writeable/readable properly.
This might also be a reason for problems like these.

Note that KDE 2.0.1 will be released next week. I've already compiled
it for Tru64 and I'm running it right now. It fixes a couple of small bugs
under Tru64 (like kmail not working or kcontrol->Look&Feel->Colors crashing).

I'll announce it here as soon as it's available next week.

