> Can anyone explain why installupdate needs you to remove some layered
> products before you upgrade a system?
> Thanks
> 
> Sent via Deja.com http://www.deja.com/
> Before you buy.

I am by no means an expert on Tru64 but this is what I gather is the
problem...

Layered products are actually installed on top of the base OS.  ie:
Open3D(problem I had earlier).  Because they actually modify the
existing OS and how it operates updating the OS would more likely than
not cause the layered suite to stop working.  Ideally I suppose the
install/update software should be able to not only detect this but also
allow the option of removal.  Perhaps this has been done in later
version but as of 4.0c-f that does not appear to be the case.

Some of the products may not halt the install but will not work
correctly if at all after the upgrade.

I think the difference is some have a more direct effect on the hardware
and kernel than others (as mentioned above Open3D or even say Sys V Env
which if I recall modifies the devices).  Perhaps this is why some need
to be removed before hand while others simply reinstalled on occasions
they no longer work.

Hope this helps and I didnt mislead anyone. 

-Jason



