Looking for a URL or the like to some good information on tweaking
network and X performance under Tru64 4.0d-f using Open3D and a
PowerStorm 4D60T.

Recently we ran a test running X applications remotely from an Ultimate
Workstation 533au2 on a DS-20. The DS-20 was using a PowerStorm 4D60T
with 32MB and 16MB(texture) and 512MB of system RAM.  All of this across
a 100base Half Duplex lan but on the same hub as the 533au2.  The
graphics performace was excellant.

Recently we are attempting to do the same with a Personal Workstation
433 128MB sys RAM and an identical Graphics card as above (PS 4D60T 32
16).  Running it across a 100base Full Duplex switched lan and both
machines on the same hub and their ports designated within the same
trunc branch. The graphics perforamce while "usable" is far below what
we experienced before.

I realize the obvious differences between the DS-20 and the old PW 433
but I would not think that the display of an X application would be
affected to this degree.  The 433 rarely hits 13% on CPU usage (ive seen
one spike in about 2hrs of use that hit 35%) and as far as I can tell
less than 10% of physical ram is in use at anytime and swamp stays at
around 33%(of approx. 250MB).

It does not appear to me that the system locally is having resource
problems.  Im also positive the server is handling this without problems
as since its resources are not only hardly touched but as mentioned
before this all worked fine on a DS-20.

The performance loss is in the form of "jerkiness" in the applications. 
They are a sort of CAD environment and as an example panning around
inside a workspace will be fine for a short distance and then halt for a
second or two then continue again.

My guess is its related to either X or the networking.  Or perhaps
both.  Either X is unable to keep up for some reason or the network
connection is slowing the transfer of information down.

In either case does anyone have suggestions?

TIA
Jason



