What I'd end up doing would be to modify the script to add -vx to the
interpreter name.  That is, on the first line, where the shell is indicated,
change it from:

        #! /sbin/sh
        
to 

        #! /sbin/sh -vx
        
to cause commands and arguments to be displayed as the lines are executed.
Then, take note of where the errors occur, and deal accordingly.

        Stu



