> > P.M.Wong (s11976@net1.hkbu.edu.hk) wrote:
> > : User accounts on our rs6k box (running aix4.3.3) will have
> > : to be copied across to an alpha running TRU64 ver.5
> > : Previously when i did shifting from 1 aix box to another
> > : , i simply copied their password lines in the
> file /etc/security/passwd
> >
> I did it for more than 200 users and, as today, nobody complained.
> AIX 4.2 -> Tru64 Unix V5.0A

I've done something similar with Solaris and NIS+ and also from AIX 4.2
to Solaris.  As long as you're talking about passwords encrypted with
crypt(), it's portable across all the UNIX platforms I've seen.

The only place you're going to run into trouble is if you're using something
other than crypt(), which is the case by default after a user has been
created on a C2 Tru64 UNIX system.  This means that going *to* Tru64 UNIX
will be relatively easy, but moving from a C2 Tru64 UNIX system to another
platform will be more work.  I've done that too, and it's not terribly
difficult, but definitely more work than going the other way.

Tim
