4100's, ES40's, and GS140's and have yet to see an adaptec SCSI card used.

If not, I would go with Intraserver(High Performance) or the Compaq
part(supported).

I am running 4.0f on a few DS20E's here, but I only have firmware 5.6
loaded.  You may want to try backing out to 5.6 or 5.7.  Additionaly, I
would reccomend 4.0f over 4.0g.  4.0f is pretty time tested and 4.0g only
adds Wildfire (GS80, GS160, GS320) support.  That was the whole point of the
"g" OS.  Our current production OS/Firmware is 4.0f with patch kit 4 and
firmware version 5.7.  (Still have not got our DS20's upgraded to 5.7)

5.8 is pretty new.

