I had the same problem,
and after investigation,
I found that the ROOT crontab was running 'rdate'
at exactly the same time as my crontab job.
If rdate puts the time back brutally a few seconds,
then my cron job gets runs twice.

(Apparently ntpd will not provoke this,
as there are no time jumps,
just the slowing down or speeding up of time
until the two machines are in sync)

Check to see if this is your situation,

Cheers,
Paul Kindervater

