Today we've got all nics hooked into the same physical switch,
so the switch becomes a single point of failure. What I'd like
to have is two switches - interconnected via a trunk port -
so that if one switch dies, the nic on the other switch
is activated.

The switch is configured into several VLANS. My DS20e
cluster will be located on VLAN-INTERNAL.

Machines on one VLAN can only communicate directly with
machines in the same VLAN. To access the other switch,
traffic is sent via the dedicated trunk port. There's
a backup trunk port, should the primary trunk port die.

