Salvador Dali (vedranvl@yahoo.com) wrote:
: How can I define VT100 keys 'Help' and 'Do' in a PC terminal emulation
: program which requires escape sequence for a key definition?

First, the VT100 didn't have a "Help" or a "Do" key.  Maybe you're thinking of
the VT2xx series and newer?

On the VT2xx series and newer terminals, the Help key was essentially function
key F15 and the Do key was F16.  Their escape sequences can be found in
SYS$SYSTEM:SMGTERMS.TXT on your nearby local VMS system. 

If you don't have a VMS system at hand (and if not, why do you want the Help
and Do keys?), the definitions are:

         F15 = "<esc>[28~"
         F16 = "<esc>[29~"
         
        Stu


