Hi,
(sorry for the delay, I just came back from a convention)

the problem was, everytime our Users tried to save something out of M$-Word
to our NetApp-Filer they would receive errors like:

- there is a file permission error, can not continue to save....
- the file is in use and can not be saved....
- Make sure that the drive is closed and contains the proper disk or CD.
- The network connection may be lost. Filename.doc

So everybody tried to blame NetApp until I found this little article on the
M$-KB, which exactly reflects the errors.
(See: Q 216077, Errors saving to a Netware Server and Q171406 How to disable
the use of UNC)
(Little note at the bottom of the page: This is known error in the
M$_....release....)


I went in to the registry down to

HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Office\8.0\Word\Options

and added a new DWORD_Value

and named it

DontUseUNC            (D U and UNC are capital_letters)

and set the Value Data to 1

And in the very same moment all the problems were gone and I was the hero if
the day ;-)

Then I added the work_around to our login-script so that all users would
have it as soon as they log in and from this day on there was not a single
phone call regarding this problem.
As soon as I change the Value_Data to 0(Zero) all the errors are back again.

Hope that helps.

Regards
Roy

