I've been able to restore vdumps without the dd command when I wrote
them with:
        vdump -0 -b 60 -f - $fs  | rsh $remote dd bs=60k of=/dev/nrmt0h
"-b 60" is the default blocking factor for vdump so the option should
not be necessary, but I put it in anyway just to be sure.  Of course
with
version 5 none of this is necessary.






