Does this assume that the system was configured for deferred swap allocation
mode?  I think our system was configured for immediate swap allocation.

My understanding of immediate swap mode is that it's the virtual process
size that drives swap space usage which made me suspicious when I saw the
differences in the VSZ column of the output from the ps command.  Perhaps it
isn't as simple as I would like to think.

There were two points that I didn't make clear in the initial posting
(a common failing of mine - sorry):
1. In reality many users executing the same application.  So, the kernel
freeing/not freeing VM when a process free()'s memory would make a real
difference on the amount of swap being used.
2. The swap space size wasn't modified by the upgrade from Tru64 3.2 to 4.0.


