Surf to http://www.csse.monash.edu.au/~jon/bqs.html. 
However, if one uses a queueing system, users don't have to rsh/ssh into
the machine on which they want to run a job. Instead one submits a job
and requests certain resources for this job (machine type, cpu time,
memory, disk space, etc.) from a 'central' or 'front-end' machine. Then
the scheduler of the queueing system decides where to run the job and
sends it to the choosen machine.
