Keith Bradnam wrote:
> 
> I recently wanted to see if I could increase the amount of diskspace
> available to a domain (and the one fileset in that domain).  Rather than
> add more volumes, I just wanted to increase the size of the existing
> partition.

Well as all of us "experts" know, "you can't get there from here"
(unless you backup the domain and all the filesets on it to tape and
start over again).  Having "been there and done that", here is some
simple advice if you plan on using AdvFS (which I highly recommend).

	Just say "No" to partitioning your disks !

Yep, don't do it, unless you are planing on have a swap partition on the
drive.  You can even put multiple filesets on the domain you use for
root !!!

What you need to realize is that FileSets are functionally the same
thing as a partition, except they are dynamic !!  Yes, you can add them,
delete them, expand them, shrink them all on a live system.  They are
fantastic !  

I will put my plug in for buying AdvFS Utilities because you can then
"addvol" on a live system !! It also works well.  I haven't had to split
a volume after creating one, but I know it can be done.

Just remember Advfs means you never have to fsck again !!! 


Jack Patteeuw



