I think 4.0 was the initial version of Tru64 that Compaq was targetting as an
Internet Server platform.  This  is probably based on the OS theory that processes
are always growing, shrinking, growing, shrinking as infinitum.  It would free the
OS to server other system calls and network I/O, rather than constantly scanning
lists that can potentially be very large.

