In article <Pine.LNX.4.30.0011140742100.14583-100000@anahata.ma.ic.ac.uk>,
andy thomas wrote:

>Does anyone know if Digital Unix ever have an audio CD player bundled with
>it?

Yes, it is in the multimedia subsystem (MMS-RT). Te filename is
/usr/bin/X11/demos/xcd. Not the most comfortable one, but it works. There
are some freeware package that also support Tru64, but we refrained from
installing them due to security considerations (all of them required setuid
root, while xcd is content with access to the cam device).

>Secondly, I assume most SCSI CD writers will work in an Alpha PWS 500au
>using one of the generic X-Windows cdrecord or cdwrite packages but has
>anyone had any experience of doing this?

Neither cdwrite nor cdrecord is X-Windows. Cdrecord, at least, works, we
have used it on a DEC 3000 with an HP CD writer.

Sure, there are X-Windows frontends for cdrecord, but I'd advise you to
first get cdrecord going from command line before you try out to get one of
the frontends working.

Kind Regards,
Tobias.



