Hello

I believe it means either use the value of $2 or -10. ie if this is in a
script called "george" and you were to run:
./george sort_this_file 27
Then it would sort "sort_this_file" and display to first 27 lines otherwise
if you ran:
./george sort_this_file
it would sort "sort_this_file" and display the first 10 lines.
${2:-10} means either use the value of $2 or if $2 is NULL use the
"default" value -10.

Hope I've explained this to your satisfaction.

Robert Mulley
Unix Admin

