Hi Andy,

Yes, 64MB is really pushing it.  That's the root cause of the problem.
However, I'd make the following changes to the UBC anyway, if for
nothing else than good tuning practice.  You're not going for
performance anyway with that little memory.  If at some later point you
find you're waiting on a disk and that the situation might be improved
with more buffer space AND you have the free physical memory to do that,
you can always increase these parameters slightly.

> ubc-minpercent = 10

Drop to 1.

> ubc-maxpercent = 100

Drop to 4.

> ubc-borrowpercent = 20

Drop to 2.

> vm-ubcseqstartpercent = 50

Drop to 3.

> vm-ubcseqpercent = 10

Drop to 2.

Note that I'm sliding the values of these parameters down as a group.
This is important if you want the VM subsystem to work as designed.

Hope the memory upgrade helps!

WJD


