It could well be the number of filehandles configured in your kernel.
You need to push them to the limit. Every samba process uses 3 filehandles (if
I remember correctly). And evrey user forks of another SambA instance.

I don't have my Alpha here in reach but when you find the kernel parameters
than you will be able to see the amount of file handles. Double them and you
are out of the problems.

And memory is certainly not the problem when you have enough viirtual memory.
It does'nt perform that good but it does work. Besides a lot of the memory from
the samba processes is resident, so the oughts that a complete new instance is
forked with it's own memory is practically 0.

Raymond

