Alright, I've got to put an end to the speculation. Sure more memory helps but it
is not the solution. It is not filehandles either, default number of file handles
is 4096, this means a possible 4096 filehandles per process. New samba process, new
number of file handles. The problem is solved by point Number 2 that I made in my
reply.

Increase the value of maxusers in your kernel config file. This is the file
/sys/conf/<HOSTNAME>.
doconfig -c HOSTNAME
cp /vmunix /vmunix.old
cp /sys/HOSTNAME/vmunix /
reboot system

This will solve your problem.

Robert.

