> setting setuid on a program or script and running the program,  will
> not change the users effective ID.

Of course not. It will only ALLOW the program in question to change it's
EUID to the SUID via system call seteuid(). Of course, a shell script
cannot call that function.

Now, I have heard that CSh, if SetUID to root itself, will change UIDs
of scripts, if they have SetUID on them. Not sure about this, though.

Nix.



