bnost@online.no writes:
>> The boot console tells me it is a Digital TGA2 graphics card installed.
>> "SuperProbe" under linux thinks it is a 512K CL-542x card.
(snip)
>> Visual inspection tell me it has a CL-5424 chip, 4 chips with -60 marking
>> which I assume are memory chips, and another 1 with -70 which also looks like
>> a memory chip. There is a standard D15 connector for the monitor and a
>> headphone minijack like output for some kind of 3D glasses sync control.

If the card is short (approx. 175mm) and if it has a chip marked
with "IBM 21-43826-01 26H3574", it is probably a DEC PowerStorm 3D30
(PBXGB-AA).  CL-GD5424 on PowerStorm 3D30 is for text mode (not for
graphics).

  http://www.support.compaq.com/open3d/SW3D30.htm

 and also my Graphic Card Compatibility List
  http://moon.hanya-n.org/comp/alpha/hct/graphics.html

>> Also, what kind of signal does Digital Unix 4.0D program it to send out? I
>> have a Nokia Multigraph 447M that can do 1280x1024, but when the CD boots
>> into the X server it just shows a flickering screen that it is unable to lock
>> onto.
>> I'd like to install DU too, but it is a bit hard when I can see anything
>> (which was why I went to linux in the first place...).

If the card is actually a PowerStorm 3D30, you can see a rotary switch
(SW1) on it. The switch is for changing the screen resolution (and maybe
some timings). Try SW1=8, C or D.

