I believe the actual problem here is with one of two things.
1. If the program in question is running as a non-root user then you might
want to check:
max-proc-per-user or max-threads-per-user. in the proc subsystem in
/etc/sysconfigtab
2. The most likely fix is that your MAXUSERS is set too low in your kernel
config file.
So cd to /sys/conf
vi your config file LYNX (?) and find the line maxusers.
Double this or set to something like 1024. Lots of other memory and process
attributes are derived from this value.

Rebuild the kernel, reboot the machine. Should handle more load.

