On Wed, 01 Nov 2000 02:27:20 +0100, Nicolas VERITE wrote:

> I got <defunct> processes that don't disappear.
> Nothing happens when I kiil -9 them...
>
> What's that ?

That's normal on a Unix system and is indicative of poorly written
application software where a process which spawns child processes
doesn't clean up after the children die.

You can't send the defunct process any signal, because the process is
dead.  It's only still taking up a slot in the process table because the
parent didn't bother to wait() for it (see the wait manual page).

I hope that helps...

